{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Take the staff and assemble.</b> Says the Rav the Bekhor Shor: it is speaking of striking the rock — He tells him to take the staff, and this is the same event as in Beshalah, where it is written there והכית בצור, except that there He arranges how He provides for Israel with manna and meat and water, and afterward explains each in its place — and both are one event, for there it is written ויקרא שם המקום מסה ומריבה, and in the parashah of VeZot HaBerakhah it is written אשר נסיתו במסה תריבהו על מי מריבה, and also here it is written המה מי מריבת קדש מדבר סין, and there too it is written ויסעו ממדבר סין. And the fact that it is written here ודברתם אל הסלע — it is not coming to exclude striking it; rather this is what it says: you shall speak to the children of Israel before the rock, so that they see the matter with their own eyes — that I am bringing forth water for them from צור החלמיש. And [regarding] what they said, שמעו נא המורים המן הסלע הזה נוציא לכם מים — that is to say: why do you contend with us? Are we able to bring forth water for you from this rock, if not by means of the Holy One, blessed be He? And if so, the way of prayer and supplication is what you should have had to request of Him, not the way of contention and complaint. And because they should have phrased their words more [carefully], the Holy One, blessed be He, was strict with them and said יען לא האמנתם בי. And according to the plain sense, the punishment is from their saying נוציא, and they should have said יוציא, which implies — the Holy One, blessed be He, brings forth. And so the paytan established: נוקש בעשר — and that is the yod of יוציא, [which is] ten."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The text appears to conflate two separate biblical episodes: the rock at Rephidim (Exodus 17, struck by Moses) and the rock at Kadesh (Numbers 20). The Bekhor Shor identifies them as one event. The paytan citation 'נוקש בעשר' could not be identified with certainty. The word תריבהו is spelled defectively in the source (missing a vav)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:47.365685522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}